    "title": "pandas.TimedeltaIndex.microseconds — pandas 2.1.4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.TimedeltaIndex.microseconds#\n\n- \n*property* TimedeltaIndex.microseconds[source]#\n- Number of microseconds (>= 0 and less than 1 second) for each element. Examples For Series: >>> ser = pd.Series(pd.to_timedelta([1, 2, 3], unit='U')) >>> ser 0 0 days 00:00:00.000001 1 0 days 00:00:00.000002 2 0 days 00:00:00.000003 dtype: timedelta64[ns] >>> ser.dt.microseconds 0 1 1 2 2 3 dtype: int32 For TimedeltaIndex: >>> tdelta_idx = pd.to_timedelta([1, 2, 3], unit='U') >>> tdelta_idx TimedeltaIndex(['0 days 00:00:00.000001', '0 days 00:00:00.000002', '0 days 00:00:00.000003'], dtype='timedelta64[ns]', freq=None) >>> tdelta_idx.microseconds Index([1, 2, 3], dtype='int32')",
    "markdown_length": 676,
